# ─── Amplify / AppSync credential overrides ───────────────────────────────────
#
# These variables are OPTIONAL.  The app reads its AppSync endpoint and API key
# from amplify/amplify_outputs.json (regenerated by `npx ampx pipeline-deploy`
# during every CI/CD build).  Set these only when you need to override that
# file — for example if the committed copy has a stale API key.
#
# In the AWS Amplify Console:  App settings → Environment variables
# For local development:       copy to .env.local (gitignored via *.local)
#
# VITE_APPSYNC_URL=https://<api-id>.appsync-api.<region>.amazonaws.com/graphql
# VITE_APPSYNC_API_KEY=da2-<your-api-key>

# ─── RDS / Lambda secrets (set in Amplify Console → Secrets, NOT here) ────────
#
# DB_HOST   MySQL host
# DB_USER   MySQL username
# DB_PASS   MySQL password
# DB_NAME   MySQL database name
# DB_PORT   MySQL port (default 3306)

# ─── Cognito Hosted UI (REQUIRED for authentication) ──────────────────────────
#
# These variables enable the Cognito Hosted UI login/logout flow.
# All five must be set for authentication to work.
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local (which is gitignored):
#      cp .env.example .env.local
#
# 2. Fill in the values from your Cognito User Pool + App Client in the AWS
#    Console (https://console.aws.amazon.com/cognito/v2/):
#
# VITE_COGNITO_REGION=us-east-1
# VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_ba4UX341U
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=<your-app-client-id>
#
# The domain is the Cognito Hosted UI domain — find it in the User Pool →
# App integration → Domain section.  Include the full hostname (no trailing /).
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=https://<your-prefix>.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com
#
# Redirect URI: must exactly match one of the "Allowed callback URLs" configured
# on the Cognito App Client.  For local dev use the Vite dev server URL:
# VITE_COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/auth/callback
#
# Logout URI: must exactly match one of the "Allowed sign-out URLs" on the App
# Client.  After sign-out Cognito will redirect here:
# VITE_COGNITO_LOGOUT_URI=http://localhost:5173
#
# For production deployments add these in the AWS Amplify Console under
# App settings → Environment variables (not in this file).

